7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:36,160
the center. Conversation 1 Welcome to Money Matters, a weekly program that helps you

8
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:37,040
manage your money.

9
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:41,640
Tonight, I'll be talking to Mary Johnson about budgeting.

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,260
Hello, everyone. There's a magic about money.

11
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:51,260
When it's not planned for, tracked, and kept a record of, it literally disappears.

12
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:55,220
What are some of the steps we can take to prevent this from happening?

13
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:58,620
Well, it's all about keeping track of your money.

14
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:03,940
If you don't do that, you'll never be able to set any goals for your budget or have

15
00:01:03,940 --> 00:01:05,520
the discipline to stick to them.

16
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:07,960
That's easier said than done.

17
00:01:08,440 --> 00:01:13,680
I read recently that only 41 of Americans adhere to a budget.

18
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:19,640
Yes, but knowing what you earn and what you spend can give you reassurance that you

19
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:21,460
won't get into debt in the first place.

20
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:26,660
You can do this by adding up all of your sources of income you have and writing them

21
00:01:26,660 --> 00:01:28,440
all down on a piece of paper.

22
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:32,480
On the same page, write down all of your monthly expenses.

23
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:36,820
I'm always amazed at how much my expenses add up.

24
00:01:36,860 --> 00:01:43,140
But designating each item as an income or an expense really helps me have a much

25
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:45,180
better sense of all my spending.

26
00:01:45,660 --> 00:01:51,460
Right. Most people have no idea how much they spend each day, let alone each week or

27
00:01:51,460 --> 00:01:54,340
month, no matter how careful they are.

28
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:57,780
Next, subtract your monthly expenses from income.

29
00:01:58,180 --> 00:02:01,400
If the result is positive, you are living within your means.

30
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:06,160
If the result is a negative number, you're going to have to cut back on your

31
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:09,120
spending. I'm usually a negative number.

32
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:13,720
I just can't resist the allure of all those prestigious goods.

33
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:18,460
Well, it's not a catastrophe, but you do have to make some changes.

34
00:02:19,260 --> 00:02:21,900
Try cutting back on those non -essential items.

35
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:28,160
Sell some stuff in your attic or shop online to avoid unnecessary temptations like

36
00:02:28,160 --> 00:02:33,640
chocolate. Failing that, you can always find yourself a part -time job.

