155
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:51,120
In America, most researchers concede that boys and girls are brought up in different

156
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:55,750
ways, taught different skills, and rewarded for different acts.

157
00:14:56,740 --> 00:15:01,320
Women, it is agreed, excel at certain tasks, men at others.

158
00:15:01,880 --> 00:15:06,680
There is little argument that some personality traits appear more dominant in one

159
00:15:06,680 --> 00:15:07,780
sex than in the other.

160
00:15:07,780 --> 00:15:13,140
All of this notwithstanding, gender differences are very much in the media these

161
00:15:13,140 --> 00:15:18,800
days. Since the rise of the women's movement, gender role behavior has come under

162
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:22,200
closer scrutiny. How has this affected friendship?

163
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:25,960
How do the sexes differ in their friendship relations?

164
00:15:26,940 --> 00:15:32,080
Most pre -teen children have a best friend who is usually someone of the same sex

165
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:33,340
and similar age.

166
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:38,560
Both sexes share an essentially positive recollection of these childhood

167
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:41,760
friendships. They do not differ in this respect.

168
00:15:42,720 --> 00:15:48,020
However, the type of engaged in during these early friendships is telling of the

169
00:15:48,020 --> 00:15:49,060
difference to come.

170
00:15:49,960 --> 00:15:53,580
Boys tend to form play groups that are competitive in nature.

171
00:15:54,100 --> 00:15:58,260
Girls groups more frequently revolve around cooperative enterprises.

172
00:15:58,260 --> 00:16:05,180
Thus, at an early age, boys become concerned with trying hard and winning, while

173
00:16:05,180 --> 00:16:10,260
girls, by contrast, play house and school, engaging in roles that require

174
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:11,740
complementary support.

175
00:16:12,700 --> 00:16:18,080
Speaking of their childhood, men recall being highly responsive to and aware of the

176
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:20,240
gender role opinions of other boys.

177
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:26,060
Girls in pre -teen years appear to be less susceptible to gender role pressure.

178
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:31,440
It is not until the dating years that women report being concerned with feminine

179
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:36,620
behavior. Males, for the most part, are responsive to the suggestion that their

180
00:16:36,620 --> 00:16:39,460
behavior is unmanly at almost any age.

181
00:16:40,280 --> 00:16:45,680
These early attitudes, reinforced by social conditioning, continue to play an active

182
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:49,380
part in the friendships of both sexes during adolescence.

183
00:16:49,380 --> 00:16:55,540
This is a period when the majority of once again report a close alliance with same

184
00:16:55,540 --> 00:17:01,420
-sex friends. Now, however, with heightened intensity, considerable energy is

185
00:17:01,420 --> 00:17:06,480
devoted to competing for position, and a definite undercurrent of competition

186
00:17:06,480 --> 00:17:08,320
permeates the relationship.

187
00:17:09,060 --> 00:17:14,700
Although in dissimilar fashion, females share equally fragile relationships at this

188
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:20,760
age. For them, the bond of loyalty extends only to the line of romantic involvement.

189
00:17:21,720 --> 00:17:26,980
This is most apt to be the case in late adolescence, when dating and relationships

190
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:30,340
with boys take sharp precedence over sisterhood.

191
00:17:31,180 --> 00:17:36,340
Actually, dating dilutes the intensity of same -sex friendships for men also.

192
00:17:37,040 --> 00:17:41,740
For the majority of us, the moment we begin to date seriously, there's a competition

193
00:17:41,740 --> 00:17:43,960
between romance and friendship.

