00:18:48,060 --> 00:18:54,600
Good afternoon. In today's lecture, we'll be talking about how and when to disclose

199
00:18:54,600 --> 00:18:57,280
a disability when applying for a job.

200
00:18:58,160 --> 00:19:03,260
On average, about 20 of the population has some form of disability.

201
00:19:03,940 --> 00:19:09,620
Most countries these days have equal opportunity and non -discrimination laws.

202
00:19:10,360 --> 00:19:17,140
Yet, disabled people often find it hard to decide when, how, and, if at all, to

203
00:19:17,140 --> 00:19:20,660
raise their disability problem with a potential employer.

204
00:19:21,360 --> 00:19:25,540
There is uncertainty about how a recruiter will perceive their disability.

205
00:19:25,540 --> 00:19:32,180
As such, many candidates fear they wouldn't be considered for a position as a of

206
00:19:32,180 --> 00:19:33,850
disclosing this personal information.

207
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:40,600
And research has validated this as a genuine concern for many job applicants.

208
00:19:41,360 --> 00:19:45,700
It's a natural reaction, but it shouldn't be a reason to stay quiet.

209
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:51,580
People need to remember that they are applying for a position they have the skills

210
00:19:51,580 --> 00:19:54,140
and experience to excel in.

211
00:19:54,140 --> 00:19:59,980
Discussing a disability with a potential employer may help them make reasonable

212
00:19:59,980 --> 00:20:02,180
workplace adjustments in their favor.

213
00:20:03,100 --> 00:20:07,820
It's most appropriate to discuss a disability when they reply to confirm an

214
00:20:07,820 --> 00:20:13,980
interview. This information needn't be put up front in their cover letter or resume

215
00:20:13,980 --> 00:20:17,680
because it's probably not relevant to the position itself.

216
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:23,300
Candidates with disabilities should feel they have the power to make their own

217
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:27,980
decisions around sharing this information free from prejudice.

218
00:20:29,140 --> 00:20:34,900
If they find an organization that doesn't celebrate diversity and inclusion, it

219
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:37,060
could say a lot about the company's culture.

220
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:40,980
Perhaps the organization isn't the right fit.

221
00:20:40,980 --> 00:20:46,580
It's important for them to remember that they are seeking a manager and employer

222
00:20:46,580 --> 00:20:51,280
that's going to be supportive and continue to give them a great employment

223
00:20:51,280 --> 00:20:57,740
experience. Companies sometimes offer candidates the chance to disclose disabilities

224
00:20:57,740 --> 00:20:59,780
on their application form.

225
00:21:00,180 --> 00:21:04,220
But people shouldn't feel restricted by this method or timing.

226
00:21:05,100 --> 00:21:08,740
People should avoid sharing the name of their disability or condition.

227
00:21:08,740 --> 00:21:14,260
There is always the risk that the recruiter will research information that is

228
00:21:14,260 --> 00:21:16,120
inaccurate or irrelevant.

229
00:21:17,260 --> 00:21:21,520
If people don't think their disability will impact their ability to perform in the

230
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:22,720
advertised position,

231
00:21:23,380 --> 00:21:29,840
then it's entirely their entitlement to choose when and whether to share this

232
